.TH ROCUTIL 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
rocUtil \- DCS register and block access to a ROC through a DTC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rocUtil
.RI [ options ]
.I operation
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends DCS request packets over the DTC's DCS DMA channel and reads the replies.
.I operation
is one of:
.TP
.B read_register
.BR ReadROCRegister (link,
.IR address ),
repeated
.B \-n
times; the value is logged through TRACE/TLOG.
.TP
.B simple_read
As
.BR read_register ,
but prints
.I "iteration value"
(value in hex with 0x) on stdout and puts TRACE in slow-only mode for the run.
.TP
.B write_register
.BR WriteROCRegister (link,
.IR address ,
.IR data )
without acknowledgement.
.TP
.BR read_extregister ", " write_extregister
Extended (firmware block) register access using
.BR \-b .
.TP
.B reset_roc
Writes 0x11 to extended register 1 of blocks 12, 11, 10, 9, 8.
.TP
.B toggle_serdes
Switches the SERDES oscillator between 2.5 and 3.125 Gbps.
.TP
.BR block_read ", " raw_block_read
Read
.B \-c
words from
.IR address .
.TP
.B block_write
Writes the
.B \-c
words 0,1,2,... to
.I address
(a test pattern, not user data).
.TP
.BR test_read ", " read_release
Read and release raw DCS DMA buffers under the DCS lock.
.SH OPTIONS
Values may be attached
.RB ( \-n5 ,
.BR \-n=5 )
or separate
.RB ( "\-n 5" );
a separate value that is not numeric and does not start with 0 is not consumed
and the option takes 0.
.TP
.BI \-l " link"
ROC link 0\-5 (default 0).
.TP
.BI \-a " address"
ROC register address.
.TP
.BI \-w " data"
Data to write.
.TP
.BI \-b " block"
Firmware block for the extended operations.
.TP
.BI \-c " count"
Word count for block operations (default 0).
.TP
.B \-i
Clear the increment-address bit for block operations.
.TP
.BI \-n " num"
Repeat count (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-d " us"
Delay between iterations.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-Q
Quiet, really quiet.
.TP
.BI \-\-dtc " n"
Card index (default
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
else 0).
.TP
.BI \-\-link\-mask " mask"
ROC mask applied when the DTC object is constructed (default 0x111111);
the nibble of
.B \-l
is always added.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout\-ms " ms"
DCS reply timeout (default 10).
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-on\-error
Stop the loop at the first exception.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage, exit 0.
The usage lists
.BR \-v ;
it is not parsed and is reported as an unknown option (usage, exit 0).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 in all handled cases, including errors logged per iteration and an
unrecognised operation.
Uncaught library exceptions (device open, DCS lock timeout) abort the process.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
.BR DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE ,
TRACE variables.
.SH WARNINGS
This tool constructs
.B DTCLib::DTC
in mode
.B DTC_SimMode_NoCFO
without
.BR skipInit .
Construction therefore reconfigures the card before the requested operation
runs, even for a read: for each of the six ROC links it enables the link if its
nibble in the ROC mask is set, otherwise disables the link and its ROC emulator;
it clears SERDES loopback and the ROC emulator on every link, and sets the
CFO-emulation bit (bit 15 of 0x9100).
Do not run it against a card that belongs to a running partition.
.PP
The DCS lock is a driver flag shared by every process on the host.
If the library cannot take it within 1 s it force-releases it (even if
another process holds it) and throws; see
.BR libDTCInterface (3).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
rocUtil \-l 0 \-a 18 simple_read
rocUtil \-\-dtc 1 \-l 2 \-a 14 \-w 0x10 write_register
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2eUtil (1),
.BR my_cntl (1),
.BR libDTCInterface (3),
.BR mu2e (4)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
